<title>GERMANY: BRAZIL'S 97/98 COFFEE CROP PEGGED AT 25 MLN BAGS.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL'S 97/98 COFFEE CROP PEGGED AT 25 MLN BAGS.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop may total 25 million bags compared with a new estimate for 1996/97 of 29 million, German trader Bernhard Rothfos GmbH said in its quarterly digest.</p>
<p>Rothfos in May put the 1997/98 crop at 24-25.5 million bags when its estimate for 1996/97 was 30 million bags.</p>
<p>Rothfos said the 1997/98 figure was made up of 20 million unwashed arabicas (24 million in 1996/97) and five million robustas (conillons) (five million 96/97).</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
